                            <comment id="494383" author="bzzz" created="Mon, 11 May 2026 11:03:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;bisection:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
9c20356df1	1	1	0		LU-18550 osd-ldiskfs: oied_name is not &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;-terminated
86b0c90666	1	0	1	BAD	LU-19712 llapi: Introduce pool pinning API
bbe23406f6	9	8	0		LU-19712 mdd: Inherit pin xattr from parent
cbb05e65e7	9	8	0		LU-19921 llite: Add user_principal &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; client mount option
31b359c11a	10	9	0		LU-20164 lnet: Return correct error on alloc_ordered_workqueue failure
90d1c7d3b5	9	8	0		LU-20061 quota: Add opiton to display root quota entry
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this is due to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-object&quot;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt; mdd_pin_init(&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; struct lu_env *env, struct mdd_object *pobj,
			struct lu_buf *pin_buf)
...
	lu_buf_alloc(pin_buf, buf_size);
	pin_buf-&amp;gt;lb_len = rc;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;then in lu_buf_init() we pass lb_len to OBD_FREE():&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;void lu_buf_free(struct lu_buf *buf)
{
	LASSERT(buf);
	&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (buf-&amp;gt;lb_buf) {
		LASSERT(buf-&amp;gt;lb_len &amp;gt; 0);
		OBD_FREE_LARGE(buf-&amp;gt;lb_buf, buf-&amp;gt;lb_len);
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;this is where math around obd_memory breaks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;introduced in commit:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;bbe23406f6 2026-03-27 | &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19712&quot; title=&quot;Add ability for admins to pin files into Pool&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19712&quot;&gt;LU-19712&lt;/a&gt; mdd: Inherit pin xattr from parent &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Nikos Papakonstantinou&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;but exposed with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;86b0c90666 2026-03-27 | &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19712&quot; title=&quot;Add ability for admins to pin files into Pool&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-19712&quot;&gt;LU-19712&lt;/a&gt; llapi: Introduce pool pinning API &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;Nikos Papakonstantinou&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

</comment>
                            <comment id="494389" author="arshad512" created="Mon, 11 May 2026 11:32:48 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 on master: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/gerrit-janitor/63511/testresults/sanity2-ldiskfs-DNE-rocky8.10_x86_64-rocky8.10_x86_64-retry1/&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/gerrit-janitor/63511/testresults/sanity2-ldiskfs-DNE-rocky8.10_x86_64-rocky8.10_x86_64-retry1/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494393" author="JIRAUSER20216" created="Mon, 11 May 2026 13:03:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, my bad. That is because I did it with different way in the first (call `mdo_xattr_get()` with NULL but first to get the size and the allocate the buffer and the call it again with the exact buffer but then there was a comment to make a &quot;large enough&quot; allocation and call it directly with the large buffer, but it seems that this left over from the previous design. So let me fix it by setting the correct buffer length in the lb_len variable.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="494397" author="gerrit" created="Mon, 11 May 2026 14:33:30 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&quot;Nikos Papakonstantinou &amp;lt;npapakonstantinou@ddn.com&amp;gt;&quot; uploaded a new patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65818&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/65818&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
